/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12752:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:30:#       depend on the new reflected geometry. Delaying recolor until post-bounce frame contact forces the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12753:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:33:#       reflected diagonals readable and removes non-essential multi-beam collisions from the training signal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12754:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:34:#     - Each accepted sample must show both signatures: at least one beam reflects multiple times, and at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12755:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:35:#       least one reflected beam actually causes a frame recolor. That prevents degeneration to D1-only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12756:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:41:#       a reflected beam's next step would hit the relevant border cells of its own frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12757:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:43:#       requires that exact revisit geometry; the visible event is the reflected return to the source-side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12758:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:50:#     - Frames remain fully inside the grid and keep a widened bounding-box clearance so long reflected beams\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12759:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:52:#     - Candidate gap sets are screened with a single-beam reflection simulator on an obstacle grid whose own\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12760:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:58:#     - The output difference is human-visible: the same block color appears both in a reflected diagonal path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12761:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:63:#     - Wider inter-frame spacing and low gap counts reduce overdraw from long reflections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12762:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:70:#     - Every chosen combo has a single-beam reflected return route that strikes its own source-side border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12763:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:72:#       with two or more reflections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12764:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:176:def _reflect_dir(d: tuple[int, int], flip_r: bool, flip_c: bool) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12765:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:185:def _reflect_pattern(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12766:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:188:    return tuple(_reflect_dir(d, flip_r, flip_c) for d in pattern)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12767:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:250:    reflection_counts: dict[int, int] = {}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:12768:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:320:        reflection_counts[bid] = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval